   "q": "Write $\\sqrt{-16}$ in terms of $i$.",
   "type": "single",
   "options": [
    "$-4$",
    "$4i$",
    "$-4i$",
    "$16i$"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "why": {
    "correct": "$i = \\sqrt{-1}$, so $\\sqrt{-16} = \\sqrt{16}\\,i = 4i$. Check: $(4i)^2 = 16i^2 = -16$.",
    "options": [
     "$(-4)^2 = 16$, not $-16$. No real number squares to a negative.",
     "Right: $\\sqrt{-16} = \\sqrt{16} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} = 4i$, and $(4i)^2 = 16i^2 = -16$.",
     "$(-4i)^2$ is also $-16$, but $\\sqrt{-16}$ names the root $4i$.",
     "Take the square root of $16$ as well: $4i$."
    ]
   }
  },
