   "why": {
    "correct": "Distribute: $3 \\cdot 1 + 3(-4i) + 2i \\cdot 1 + 2i(-4i) = 3 - 12i + 2i - 8i^2$. Since $i^2 = -1$, this is $3 + 8 - 10i = 11 - 10i$.",
    "options": [
     "Right: $3 - 12i + 2i - 8i^2 = 3 - 10i + 8 = 11 - 10i$.",
     "$-8i^2 = -8(-1) = +8$, so the real part is $3 + 8 = 11$.",
     "This multiplies only first terms and last terms; distribute all four products.",
     "The $i$ terms are $-12i + 2i = -10i$."
