    "$x = -4 \\pm 6i$",
    "$x = -2 \\pm 3i$"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "why": {
    "correct": "$b^2 - 4ac = 16 - 52 = -36$, and $\\sqrt{-36} = 6i$. So $x = \\frac{-4 \\pm 6i}{2} = -2 \\pm 3i$.",
    "options": [
     "The formula starts with $-b = -4$, so the real part is $-2$.",
     "$\\sqrt{-36} = 6i$, not $6$; the solutions are not real.",
     "Divide every term by $2a = 2$: $\\frac{-4 \\pm 6i}{2} = -2 \\pm 3i$.",
     "Right: $\\frac{-4 \\pm \\sqrt{16 - 52}}{2} = \\frac{-4 \\pm 6i}{2}$."
    ]
   }
